diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8c747b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static page with cross-window message and navigation validation.
+
+Set `ORDERING_ORIGIN` in `origin-validation.mjs` to the actual HTTPS ordering
+service before deployment. The reserved `.example` default grants no production
+service access. Ordering messages use `{ type: 'order-status', message: string }`
+or `{ type: 'redirect', url: string }`. Only that exact origin is trusted;
+redirects must additionally resolve to the page's schemeful site. Status strings
+are limited to 200 characters and rendered as text.
+
+The local iframe uses `sandbox="allow-scripts"` without `allow-same-origin`.
+Only its initial `init` message can pin its sender identity. It may subsequently
+send `{ type: 'recommendation', message: string }`, but cannot issue ordering
+commands. Other iframe windows cannot initialize or replace this pin.
+
+When available, the browser's `Origin` API provides public-suffix-aware same-site
+checks and preserves the opaque sender identity of real message events. Without
+it, redirects are restricted to the exact page origin and widget messages require
+the expected `contentWindow` plus an opaque serialized origin. This fallback
+cannot distinguish documents navigating within that same window, so the widget
+is loaded only from the fixed local resource and must not navigate to untrusted
+content. Native opaque identity is never reconstructed from the string `"null"`.
+
+Links are classified as internal or external using the same site policy;
+external web links remain usable and receive `external noopener noreferrer`.
+Non-HTTP(S) links and credential-bearing URLs are blocked at activation.
+
+Run `npm test` for Node regression tests. Native `Origin` paths use a contract
+double because Node does not expose browser-dispatched opaque origins; these
+tests do not substitute for browser interoperability testing.
